abstract: >
  Constraint is a public research and protocol alpha for testing the rules that
  turn external evidence into bounded financial claims. The public lab combines
  aggregate historical policy replay, binding-constraint attribution, stress
  replays, browser-side aggregate-bundle verification, deterministic evidence
  normalization, provenance classification, versioned policy decisions, bounded
  claim manifests, and explicit settlement shortfall accounting. SolarPunk/SPK
  remains a Sepolia reference application that motivated the generalized
  protocol. Constraint does not claim production risk adequacy, legal collateral
  rights, reserve custody, production oracle finality, or mainnet readiness.
